From: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] build: bundle the LynxI PCS without mainline MT7530

Linux 6.18 makes PCS_MTK_LYNXI a hidden symbol selected by the mainline
MT7530 MDIO frontend.  That switch driver cannot coexist with this EN751221
fork because both export the same MT7530 symbols.  Build the unmodified PCS
source as a private module in this bundle instead.  Include the hidden bool
PHY_COMMON_PROPS in that same module, matching the dependency normally selected
by PCS_MTK_LYNXI.

Signed-off-by: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>

--- a/Kbuild
+++ b/Kbuild
@@ -1,4 +1,6 @@
 obj-m := econet-eth.o econet-gsw.o econet-gsw-mdio.o econet-gsw-mmio.o mtk-tag.o
+obj-m += pcs-mtk-lynxi.o
+pcs-mtk-lynxi-y := pcs-mtk-lynxi-core.o phy-common-props.o
 econet-eth-y := econet_eth.o econet_eth_debug.o econet_qdma.o econet_port.o
 econet-gsw-y := gsw/mt7530.o
 econet-gsw-mdio-y := gsw/mt7530-mdio.o
